{{!-- First-party page written for Volta (Qompass AI, 2026). --}}
{{#> layout }}
  <h2>{{ text "Privacy" }}</h2>

  <h3>Public Key Data</h3>
  <p>
    A keyserver exists to publish public keys. Everything Volta serves —
    the key material itself, user IDs, and the addresses an owner has
    verified — is public by design and can be retrieved by anyone. Do not
    upload a key you do not want to be public.
  </p>

  <h3>What is stored</h3>
  <p>
    Uploaded keys are stored as submitted. An address becomes searchable
    only after its owner confirms it through the verification email;
    unverified addresses are not published. Verification and management
    links are sent by email and expire.
  </p>

  <h3>Removal</h3>
  <p>
    From the <a href="/manage">manage page</a>, a key owner can unpublish
    any verified address. Once every address of a key is unpublished, the
    key is no longer distributed. Note that copies other people have
    already downloaded cannot be recalled — that is a property of public
    key distribution, not of this service.
  </p>

  <h3>Server logs</h3>
  <p>
    Requests are logged for operations and abuse prevention and are not
    sold or shared for advertising.
  </p>
{{/layout}}
